From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] intel/jay: use mesa's PACKED macro for jay_predication

jay_predication is the only enum in jay_ir.h declared with C23's fixed
underlying type; every other enum in the file uses mesa's own PACKED
macro to get the same one-byte representation. GCC only understands the
C23 form from version 13 onwards, so the host build fails with

    jay_ir.h:582:22: error: expected identifier or '(' before ':' token

on distributions whose host compiler is older - Debian 12 ships GCC 12 -
and takes host-mesa3d down with it, which every mesa driver needing the
precompiled-shader compiler (iris, crocus, panfrost, asahi) depends on.

PACKED expands to __attribute__((packed)), so the enum keeps its
single-byte size and the surrounding static_asserts on packed struct
sizes continue to hold.

--- a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_ir.h
+++ b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_ir.h
@@ -580,6 +580,6 @@
 }
 
-enum jay_predication : uint8_t {
+enum PACKED jay_predication {
    /** No predication. */
    JAY_NOT_PREDICATED = 0,
 
